HST Office: the Sheets ribbon takes the layout of the approved 1.0.2 mockup (hinh-mau-sheets.html, owner 15/11/2026).

Home: Clipboard is a large Paste beside a 3-row column of labelled Cut, Copy and Format Paintbrush (Paste Special
is in Paste's ▾ menu, so its separate button goes); Font is two rows (font, size, grow/shrink, clear formatting /
B I U S, sub- and superscript, border, fill and font colour); Styles is Conditional Formatting ▾, Format as
Table and the cell styles gallery (.uno:StylesPreview, which shows Calc's cell styles with
hst-ribbon-mockup-gallery-combos.patch; it replaces the Cell Styles ▾ menu); Alignment drops the hidden right-to-left and
left-to-right buttons (owner decision) and puts Decrease Indent before Increase Indent; Cells and Editing
fill three rows (AutoSum ▾, a column of Fill ▾ and Clear ▾, Sort and Filter ▾, Find and Select ▾). Insert: the
chart types stand in one 3-row column between Chart and Sparkline (now large); Text is Text Box and Header and
Footer large beside two 3-row columns (Fontwork, Signature Line, Object / Vertical Text, Date, Time). Extensions
groups the HST tools as the mockup does: Text (administrative document, Remove Diacritics, Split Name, Sort by
Given Name), Vietnamese Formats (VND, date, percent), Data (Import CSV, Delete Blank Rows), Vietnamese Tools
(Number to Words, Convert Encoding), HASON TECH (Solutions, USB Token setup). Every other tab: large buttons fill
the three rows and small buttons stand in even 3-row columns (the mockup's grid()), captions under the rows,
separators 4 rows high. The ribbon's root box has no margin above, below or right of it (frame geometry, P4).
Every group keeps its id (the adaptive ladders apply); every command keeps its KeyTip except Cell Styles ▾ (J),
which the regenerated KeyTip table gives to the gallery. Needs hst-ribbon-mockup-gallery-combos.patch before it.

